ndy Lane stadium."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1061, "end": 1156, "text": "One of the earliest pieces of evidence that supports Brown's affiliation with Worksop Town F.C."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1157, "end": 1219, "text": "can be found in the club's archives from the 1990-1991 season."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1220, "end": 1400, "text": "A team sheet from a match against local rivals, Gainsborough Trinity, lists Grant Brown as a starting defender, alongside his future long-time partner in the backline, Mark Carter."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1401, "end": 1539, "text": "This early appearance not only demonstrates Brown's integration into the team but also sets the stage for his eventual rise to prominence."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1540, "end": 1598, "text": "As the seasons passed, Brown's influence on the team grew."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1599, "end": 1730, "text": "He became known for his unwavering commitment, his ability to read the game, and his uncanny knack for popping up with vital goals."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1731, "end": 1816, "text": "In the 1993-1994 season, Brown's contributions were instrumental in Worksop Town F.C."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1817, "end": 1885, "text": "'s promotion to the Premier Division of the Northern Premier League."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1886, "end": 2008, "text": "A newspaper clipping from the Worksop Guardian, dated April 1994, highlights Brown's heroics in a 2-1 win over Buxton F.C."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2009, "end": 2045, "text": "The article quotes Worksop Town F.C."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2046, "end": 2191, "text": "'s manager at the time, Steve Ludlam, praising Brown's \"inspirational performance\" and noting that his goal was \"the turning point in the match.\""}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2192, "end": 2249, "text": "Further evidence of Brown's tenure with Worksop Town F.C."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 157, "text": "As the sun dipped below the horizon, casting a warm orange glow over the quaint Belarusian town of Smolevichi, Grant Brown made his way to the local stadium."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 158, "end": 276, "text": "The air was alive with the sweet scent of blooming lilacs, and the sound of children's laughter carried on the breeze."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 277, "end": 383, "text": "It was a peaceful evening, one that belied the intensity of the training session that was about to unfold."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 384, "end": 524, "text": "Grant, a seasoned English footballer with a rugged charm and a thatch of sandy-blond hair, had been with FC Smolevichi for a few months now."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 525, "end": 701, "text": "He had been drawn to the club's rich history and its passionate fan base, who packed the stadium with a fervor that rivaled the most dedicated supporters in the Premier League."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 702, "end": 850, "text": "As he changed into his kit, Grant couldn't help but think about the conversation he had with the club's manager, Viktor Kuznetsov, earlier that day."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 851, "end": 1037, "text": "Viktor, a gruff but fair man with a bushy mustache and a penchant for quoting Soviet-era philosophers, had been impressed with Grant's performance in the last match against Dinamo Minsk."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1038, "end": 1129, "text": "\"You have the heart of a Belarusian, Grant,\" he had said, his eyes twinkling with approval."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1130, "end": 1164, "text": "\"You will lead us to victory, da?\""}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1165, "end": 1214, "text": "Grant smiled to himself as he laced up his boots."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1215, "end": 1362, "text": "He had always been a team player, but there was something about FC Smolevichi that made him feel like he was part of something bigger than himself."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1363, "end": 1418, "text": "Maybe it was the way the fans chanted his name, \"Grant!"}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1419, "end": 1425, "text": "Grant!"}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1426, "end": 1433, "text": "Grant!\""}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1434, "end": 1545, "text": "whenever he took the field, or the way his teammates welcomed him with open arms, despite the language barrier."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1546, "end": 1743, "text": "As he jogged out onto the pitch, Grant was greeted by the familiar sight of the FC Smolevichi crest emblazoned on the team's banner: a stylized image of a bear, symbolizing strength and resilience."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1744, "end": 1844, "text": "He felt a surge of pride and belonging, knowing that he was now a part of this tight-knit community."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1845, "end": 1924, "text": "The training session was intense, with Viktor pushing the team to their limits."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1925, "end": 2020, "text": "Grant worked tirelessly, his muscles screaming in protest as he sprinted up and down the pitch."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start"